I'm sorry folks, I don't mean to be mean, and it's really not that bad of an
idea, it's just that I find it so darn funny....

Pansy the Elf (strength=5) is roaming the dungeons, thinking he's got a
chance of making it even to level 3, when he is beset upon by a Fearsome
Goblin!

The goblin swings his dagger --more--
The goblin hits!
"Oh yeah?  Wol I'll show yew!" exclaimes Pansy in his best Tolkienesque
pseudo-British accent.

#grab

Pansy:  "Arrrrrumph!  Hmmmmmmmf!  *whew*  You're pretty 'eavy, lad."
Goblin:  "Just what the blazes do you think you're trying to do??"
Pansy:  "Why I'm gonna grab yew and I'm gonna stuff yew in my sack!"
Goblin, almost as amused as he is confused:  "What in heaven's name for?"
Pansy:  "So that later on, when I'm feeling a mite bit 'ungry, I can eat ya!"
Goblin:  "Good Lord!  How barbaric!  That's absolutely disgusting!  Why,
you're one of the most uncivilized people I've ever met!  Really!  Ugh!"
Pansy, feeling a mite bit silly, and ashamed, sets the Goblin down.  Well
OK, the Goblin is already down, never went up, so Pansy just lets go.  "I--
I'm sorry.  Boy do I feel like a real fool now.  Uh, look, can we, um, just
kind of forget that this whole incident ever happened?  If the other blokes
ever found out about this...."
Goblin, with a friendly smile, and just a hint of supreme evil in his eye:
"Don't worry, ol' chap, no-one will ever know."
Pansy:  "Gee thanks, I really appre--"
Goblin:  "Sucker." as he withdraws the blood-stained dagger.  "Hey Grog!
Nook!  Supper!"

And so equilibrium returns to the Dungeon once more as another foolish
adventurer enters the Pearly Gates of /dev/null.
